/*
  LARP CHARM firmware v9.5
  Board : Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-1.69 (240x280 ST7789V2, CST816T touch)
  Control: Bluetooth LE from the Larp Charm web app

  Home is a live tmux session: panes labelled with the command that prints them ($ date, $ np, $ ps pet,
  $ imu --scope, $ cat motd), the charm's own event log tailed like `dmesg -w`, and a status bar of
  windows. Tap a pane and the prompt types `open <pane>` before it zooms in. Tap the status bar for the
  window chooser: every screen, two big columns, like tmux's `prefix w`.
  Swipe down (or the side button) closes whatever is open.

  Blocks: weather (`curl wttr.in`: ASCII-art skies and a critter dressed for them), tty (a kaomoji in the terminal), cc (Claude Code: a live remote through larp-bridge, or a demo), clock, spotify (a terminal music player), spells and the wand (cast spells with a 1D CNN on the charm, teach your own, twist it like a knob, draw in the air, see the fingerprint map), spell recorder, eyes, jukebox, pet, dice, message, photo, ID card, torch,
          and a charging screen that appears when you plug it in.

  Touch:
    swipe left / right  -> deck home: colour theme · clock: backdrop · music: next / previous
                           eyes: expression · jukebox: next shelf · message: style
    tap                 -> clock: style (double tap 12/24h) · music: keys prev / play-pause / next, volume row - / +
                           eyes: react (double tap: love) · jukebox: queue a song · pet: pat · dice: roll
    swipe up / down on home -> brightness
    press and hold      -> the ID card
  Shake: home / clock = next backdrop · pet = dizzy · eyes = dizzy · dice = roll · jukebox = shuffle · asleep = wake
  PWR button: short = back home (on home: screen off), hold 2 s = power off (battery only)

  Files in this sketch: LarpCharm.ino and the numbered tabs 01_sensors.ino ... 20_setup_loop.ino (joined in name
  order; the map is in docs/firmware.md), spells_engine.h, spells_model.h (generated by firmware/tools/spells/train.py),
  songs.h (public-domain melodies, generated by firmware/tools/songs.py)
  Libraries (Library Manager):
    GFX Library for Arduino (moononournation) 1.6.x
    NimBLE-Arduino (h2zero) 2.x
    JPEGDEC (Larry Bank) 1.x
  Board package: esp32 by Espressif 3.x  ·  Board: ESP32S3 Dev Module
  Tools: USB CDC On Boot Enabled · Flash 16MB · PSRAM OPI
         Partition Scheme: 16M Flash (3MB APP/9.9MB FATFS)
*/

